TEXT 16 904 Left 3 ;5  Simulation setup (T110-T112 generic models)
TEXT 3416 1696 Left 4 ;Graupner/Grundig varioprop C6  SSM 27  (Best.-Nr. 3953)
TEXT 3416 1752 Left 2 ;Transmitter RF section: osc T111 / driver T112 / PA T113 / regulator T110
TEXT 3416 1792 Left 2 ;Source: schematic redraw JMF 09/13 (rc-network wiki). L, crystal, antenna = assumptions
TEXT 3416 1832 Left 2 ;State BEFORE repair: T113 = NEC 2SC1589 (estimated model), R119 = 22 R
TEXT 3416 1872 Left 2 ;T110-T112: generic NPN models (real parts: 2SC945, 2SC735-Y)
TEXT 2568 560 Left 2 ;T108 modulator (ideal stand-in)\nreal: T108 switches driver supply VDRV from coder pulses\nhere: constant {VMOD}=5 V -> carrier always ON\nRMOD = 15-20 R (T108 collector resistor, original)
TEXT 3872 1320 Left 2 ;coder T101-T108\nload only assumed placeholder
TEXT 816 280 Center 2 ;Qz1 27 MHz (sim model, Q~1000)
TEXT 5240 -40 Left 2 ;Antenna Model\nwhip ~1 m:\nR = radiation + loss\nC = rod capacitance (assumed)\nRLK = only sim dc op
TEXT 4328 48 Left 2 ;Pi-Filter\nMatching\nLow Pass\nRLK = only sim dc op
TEXT 3720 528 Left 2 ;Autotransformer\nLow Impedance at TAP\nHigh Impedance at HOT
TEXT 4760 1480 Left 2 ;Voltage Regulator to 5.5V\nFor modulators and oscillator\nOutput stage runs on VBat
TEXT 3488 -200 Left 2 ;An Online Schematic stated 4.7Ohm \nbut 22 was measured for R119.
